{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#549","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#549","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#549\",\"parent_revision\":\"0f2ef8fa343a7ccc7f885cb8a007ca829ea46ed1\",\"root_revision\":\"819c7b35a8c9c6df37d5eea66bd90958bf5394f7617f368979d936682e182a0e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEstablish a COMPAT annotation standard for all compatibility shims, fallbacks, and temporary workarounds in the codebase. Every fallback must document why it exists, what condition allows removal, and when it was added. A pre-commit hook scans for COMPAT annotations and fails CI when removal conditions are met or annotations are malformed. Companion: ADR records in .claude/decisions/ for architectural decisions that motivated the fallback. Motivated by claim-task fix (2026-03-07) which added a silent field-name fallback with no removal condition documented.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: A pre-commit hook scans for COMPAT annotations\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: scripts/check_compat_annotations.py exists and is wired as a pre-commit hook\\n- evidence: File read confirms implementation; .pre-commit-config.yaml line 153-155 confirms wiring\\n- source: scripts/check_compat_annotations.py (full file), .pre-commit-config.yaml:153-155\\n\\n**Claim 2**: Fails CI when annotations are malformed\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: Hook exits 1 when COMPAT annotation is missing required field (issue=, remove_when=, added=)\\n- evidence: check_compat_annotation() returns error message; main() returns 1 on any error\\n- source: scripts/check_compat_annotations.py:31-46, 134-160\\n\\n**Claim 3**: Fails CI when removal conditions are met\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n- claim: CI fails automatically when a remove_when condition is observable\\n- evidence: Current implementation only validates annotation format. No code evaluates whether the remove_when condition has been satisfied. The check_compat_annotation() function checks for field presence, not field semantics.\\n- source: scripts/check_compat_annotations.py:31-46\\n\\n**Claim 4**: Companion ADR records in .claude/decisions/\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: ADR-011 documents the standard; ADR-010 references it\\n- evidence: .claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md exists with Status: Accepted\\n- source: .claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md:1-71\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: COMPAT annotation standard \u2014 structured fallback tracking with CI enforcement\\nDate: 2026-04-17\\nGoal: Establish a verified, CI-enforced annotation convention for all compatibility shims so they can be tracked to removal.\\nConditions:\\n1. Pre-commit hook script exists at scripts/check_compat_annotations.py | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. ADR-011 accepted at .claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Hook wired in .pre-commit-config.yaml (id: check-compat-annotations, line 153) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. CI runs the hook via prek run --all-files (code-quality.yml, not skipped) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Annotation format defined: COMPAT(issue=#N, remove_when=\\\"...\\\", added=YYYY-MM-DD) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. At least one conforming COMPAT annotation in production: task_format.py:81 | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. Bare fm.get(\\\"task\\\") regression guard implemented in the same script | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. All existing Python files scanned for pre-ADR-011 untracked shims | Status: DERIVABLE\\n9. \\\"Fails CI when removal conditions are met\\\" \u2014 automated semantic check | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 7\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **compat annotation standard \u2014 structured fallback tracking with ci enforcement** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 claim-task fix introduced silent compatibility shim with no removal tracking\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-17)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 enforcement infrastructure is in place but the semantic removal-condition check is missing. Low urgency since annotations are actively enforced for format correctness.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a developer introduces a compatibility shim:\\n1. They write a COMPAT annotation immediately before the shim code\\n2. The annotation contains issue=, remove_when=, and added= fields\\n3. Pre-commit rejects the commit if any field is missing\\n4. CI fails the PR if any COMPAT annotation is malformed\\n5. A future reviewer can read the remove_when condition and evaluate whether the shim is still needed\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [x] `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` exists and validates COMPAT annotation format\\n- [x] Hook is wired in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` with `types: [python]`\\n- [x] CI runs the hook without skipping it\\n- [x] ADR-011 documents the annotation format and field semantics\\n- [x] At least one conforming COMPAT annotation exists in the codebase\\n- [ ] All Python files audited for pre-ADR-011 untracked shims (scan and retrofit or document)\\n- [ ] Automated removal-condition check implemented OR acceptance criteria updated to reflect that semantic checking is out of scope and manual review is the process\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md` \u2014 authoritative spec\\n- `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` \u2014 reference implementation\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNone \u2014 all infrastructure is already in place.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nS \u2014 pre-audit scan of all Python files for pre-ADR-011 shims is a one-session Grep + review task. Semantic removal-condition checking is a separate decision (in-scope or documented as manual process).\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (must carry COMPAT annotations on shims)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_format.py:81` \u2014 only current COMPAT-annotated shim in codebase\\n- Any future Python file introducing a compatibility shim\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the enforcement interface)\\n\\n- `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` \u2014 validates COMPAT annotation format and bare fm.get(\\\"task\\\") patterns; invoked by pre-commit hook\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml:153-155` \u2014 hook entry `check-compat-annotations`; types: [python]\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 runs `prek run --all-files`; check-compat-annotations is not in SKIP list\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nEstablish a COMPAT annotation standard for all compatibility shims, fallbacks, and temporary workarounds so that every shim is traceable to a GitHub issue, has a documented removal condition, and fails CI if the annotation is malformed.\\n\\n**Status as of 2026-04-17**: Core infrastructure is complete.\\n- `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` implements the format checker and bare `fm.get(\\\"task\\\")` regression guard\\n- ADR-011 documents the standard (accepted 2026-03-07)\\n- Hook wired in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` and runs in CI via `code-quality.yml`\\n- One conforming annotation exists: `task_format.py:81`\\n\\n**Remaining gap**: The description states the hook should \\\"fail CI when removal conditions are met\\\". The current implementation validates annotation format only. Automated semantic evaluation of `remove_when` conditions is not implemented.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md` \u2014 documents the format; needs updating if format changes\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-010-task-file-field-name-standard.md` \u2014 references ADR-011 as prerequisite\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Hook script exists and validates format\\n- [x] Hook wired to pre-commit\\n- [x] CI runs the check\\n- [x] ADR documents the standard\\n- [ ] All Python files scanned for pre-ADR-011 untracked shims\\n- [ ] Automated removal-condition checking implemented\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` \u2014 enforcement script\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml:153-155` \u2014 hook wiring\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 CI runner\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md` \u2014 standard definition\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-010-task-file-field-name-standard.md` \u2014 references ADR-011\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_format.py:81` \u2014 example annotation\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The codebase had no mechanism preventing silent accumulation of untracked compatibility shims. When the claim-task fix added a field-name fallback (2026-03-07), no tooling existed to document the removal condition or link to a tracking issue. The system allowed undocumented shims to be merged without constraint.\\n**Analysis Method**: no-analysis (missing-guardrail type)\\n**Scenario Target**: Untracked compatibility shim added in hotfix \u2192 COMPAT annotation standard with CI enforcement prevents accumulation\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `scripts/check_compat_annotations.py` \u2192 pre-commit enforcement\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2192 hook wiring\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2192 CI runner\\n- `.claude/decisions/ADR-011-compat-annotation-standard.md` \u2192 authoritative spec\\n\",\"digest\":\"4751491a9cfbbebf72219a0d3a0671d945610eee47a0a0fa44ef337fe4bbd8e2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgzSeA\"}"}